# Building TableTool

## Language

ISO C17. No third-party libraries. Standard C library only.

## Source files

Product sources under `src/`:

- main.c =E2=80=94 CLI entry
- utf8.c / utf8.h =E2=80=94 UTF-8 validation and traversal
- mem.c / mem.h =E2=80=94 checked allocation helpers
- table.c / table.h =E2=80=94 table model, cells, types
- parse_csv.c =E2=80=94 CSV parser/writer
- parse_tsv.c =E2=80=94 TSV parser/writer
- parse_md.c =E2=80=94 Markdown table parser/writer
- script.c / script.h =E2=80=94 batch script lexer/parser
- ops.c =E2=80=94 command execution
- url.c =E2=80=94 URL validation/normalization
- ean.c =E2=80=94 EAN-13
- code128.c =E2=80=94 Code 128 B/C encoder
- svg.c =E2=80=94 barcode SVG sheet
- report.c =E2=80=94 run report
- util.c =E2=80=94 helpers

Headers may live in `src/` or `include/`.

## Example compile

```bash
cc -std=3Dc17 -Wall -Wextra -O2 -o tabletool \
  src/main.c src/utf8.c src/mem.c src/table.c \
  src/parse_csv.c src/parse_tsv.c src/parse_md.c \
  src/script.c src/ops.c src/url.c src/ean.c \
  src/code128.c src/svg.c src/report.c src/util.c -lm
```

(Some math may be unused</span><span class=3D"text-fg-primary">; </span><sp=
an class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-command)">`-lm`</span><span class=3D"text=
-(--desktop-shell-args)"> is safe.)

## Tests

```bash
cc -std=3Dc17 -Wall -Wextra -O2 -o run_tests tests/test_main.c \
  src/utf8.c src/mem.c src/table.c src/parse_csv.c src/parse_tsv.c \
  src/parse_md.c src/url.c src/ean.c src/code128.c src/util.c -lm
./run_tests
```

Or run the acceptance scripts after building `tabletool`.

## Optional Makefile

A simple Makefile may be present for convenience</span><span class=3D"text-=
fg-primary">; </span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-command)">it</spa=
n><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-args)"> is not required.
